{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504426,"nonce":"D4Iw+bgbADQVLIqEIQ0SDipBLpM=","title":"The token system covers exactly one axis: 285 font sizes and 57 radii are bracket literals with no token behind them","was":"**What is wrong.** `web/src/index.css`'s `@theme inline` block (`:12-71`) maps **every** colour the design system owns — 15 chrome tokens, 24 state tokens across six states, 7 chart tokens — plus `--font-sans` (`:13`) and `--font-mono` (`:15`). It defines no `--text-*` and no `--radius-*`. The consequence is that font size and corner radius are the two axes with no vocabulary, and every component invents a px literal in a bracket: **285 `text-[Npx]` across 32 files** and **57 `rounded-[Npx]`**. Not one named size utility (`text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base`, …) appears anywhere in `web/src`."}]}